ar:CTX_ISSUE_122 a ar:ContextSource ;
  ar:clauseId "CTX_ISSUE_122" ;
  ar:title "Issue #122" ;
  ar:sourcePath "corpus/issue-122.json" ;
  ar:sourceStart "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> ;
  ar:sourceEnd "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> ;
  ar:charCount "1200"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> ;
  ar:excerpt "## Parent\n\n#121 — spec: Expected-set entry resolves its skill files\n\n## What to build\n\nAn Expected-set entry resolves and exposes every skill file it owns — the root `SKILL.md`, each runtime variant's `SKILL.md`, and each variant that ships an `agent.toml` instead of a `SKILL.md`. A caller can read which files an entry owns and which one failed, without rebuilding the source layout itself. The entry-level resolution status is left in place for existing callers at this stage; the skill-file facts are the new, authoritative surface.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Enumerating a fixture whose entry is fully resolved returns a skill file for the root fallback and one per variant, each carrying its variant, its resolved path, its kind (a skill file vs. an agent definition), and its own resolution status.\n- [ ] Skill files are returned in a deterministic order — root fallback first, then variants in the runtime-variant order — asserted at the enumerator's interface.\n- [ ] An entry whose source directory is missing reports its owned skill file(s) as missing with a reason that names the expected location.\n- [ ] An entry whose source directory exists but whose root `SKILL.md` is absent repor" .
ar:CTX_ISSUE_122 ar:forTask "T122" .
ar:CTX_ISSUE_123 a ar:ContextSource ;
  ar:clauseId "CTX_ISSUE_123" ;
  ar:title "Issue #123" ;
  ar:sourcePath "corpus/issue-123.json" ;
  ar:sourceStart "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> ;
  ar:sourceEnd "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> ;
  ar:charCount "1200"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> ;
  ar:excerpt "## Parent\n\n#121 — spec: Expected-set entry resolves its skill files\n\n## What to build\n\nValidation stops shadowing the Expected-set entry and stops rebuilding the source layout. It builds one list of validation targets that carries entry identity, the resolved skill file path, and the result together, so verdicts and the report cannot misalign and a missing skill file always fails the gate. The codex variant status becomes a pure projection of the enumerated file list.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Validation run end-to-end on a fixture produces the expected verdict for each entry state — fully resolved, missing source directory, missing root `SKILL.md`, malformed provenance, and a variant that ships only `agent.toml` — and the report names the file that failed.\n- [ ] Validation targets and their results are one list; no parallel arrays or positional pairing remain in the validation module.\n- [ ] A variant that ships `agent.toml` and no `SKILL.md` is reported as an informational status derived from the enumerated files, not as a failure and not by re-walking the filesystem.\n- [ ] The codex variant status projection no longer scans skill directories and no longer takes the caller's " .
ar:CTX_ISSUE_123 ar:forTask "T123" .
ar:CTX_ISSUE_124 a ar:ContextSource ;
  ar:clauseId "CTX_ISSUE_124" ;
  ar:title "Issue #124" ;
  ar:sourcePath "corpus/issue-124.json" ;
  ar:sourceStart "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> ;
  ar:sourceEnd "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> ;
  ar:charCount "1200"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> ;
  ar:excerpt "## Parent\n\n#121 — spec: Expected-set entry resolves its skill files\n\n## What to build\n\nDeployment stops reading a directory-level resolution status and judges each entry by the skill files it owns. A partial checkout stays usable for development, and a release refuses to ship when any expected skill file is missing — including the case where a skill directory exists but its root `SKILL.md` was deleted.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The development provisioning flow warns about and skips an entry with a missing skill file, and keeps provisioning every resolved entry exactly as before (partial checkout remains usable).\n- [ ] Packaging fails when any expected skill file is missing, and the error names every missing file — including the \"directory exists, root `SKILL.md` missing\" state.\n- [ ] Packaging still refuses to ship on a missing source directory and on a malformed lock file, naming the offending lock file.\n- [ ] Tarball layout, `manifest.json` content, and installed file layout are unchanged; contents and manifest still derive from one enumeration.\n- [ ] Existing development and packaging tests stay green, with new coverage for the missing-root-`SKILL.md` case; any fixture tha" .
ar:CTX_ISSUE_124 ar:forTask "T124" .
ar:CTX_ISSUE_125 a ar:ContextSource ;
  ar:clauseId "CTX_ISSUE_125" ;
  ar:title "Issue #125" ;
  ar:sourcePath "corpus/issue-125.json" ;
  ar:sourceStart "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> ;
  ar:sourceEnd "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> ;
  ar:charCount "1200"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> ;
  ar:excerpt "## Parent\n\n#121 — spec: Expected-set entry resolves its skill files\n\n## What to build\n\nThe toolkit-setup procedure and its integration suite read the enumerator's skill-file facts instead of re-deriving what the Expected set contains. The procedure stops carrying its own dialect for expected names and per-variant instruction files, and the suite asserts the shipped contract through the enumerator's interface.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The toolkit-setup integration suite asserts the enumerator's skill-file facts for the repo tree — every entry resolves all its skill files, file order is deterministic, and the entry order guarantee still holds — with no reference to the entry-level resolution status.\n- [ ] The toolkit-setup procedure instructs the agent to read the enumerated facts (which entries exist, which files each owns, which are agent definitions) rather than re-deriving expected names and per-variant files from the lock files and directory scan.\n- [ ] The procedure still reports the same outcomes for a healthy checkout: every shared entry present, exactly one router `SKILL.md` per coupled skill, runtime instruction files present, codex agent links verified, principles li" .
ar:CTX_ISSUE_125 ar:forTask "T125" .
ar:CTX_ISSUE_126 a ar:ContextSource ;
  ar:clauseId "CTX_ISSUE_126" ;
  ar:title "Issue #126" ;
  ar:sourcePath "corpus/issue-126.json" ;
  ar:sourceStart "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> ;
